## Reckons.AI — Review v0.2.9
## GENERATED by scripts/offline/release-review-space.ts (F34.5). Do not edit by hand: change the roadmap or
## the Testing graph and run `npx tsx scripts/offline/release-review-space.ts`. `--check` fails when stale.

@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ktype: <urn:kbase:type/> .
@prefix p:     <urn:kbase:predicate/> .
@prefix kmeta: <urn:kbase:meta/> .
@prefix hnav:  <urn:reckons:nav/> .
@prefix rev:   <urn:reckons:review/0.2.9/> .

rev:release rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Review v0.2.9" ;
    rdfs:comment "The visual tests of v0.2.9, in the order a person would review them. 4 of this release's 16 parts have a TestWorkflow (23 steps, each a screenshot and what the test checks); 13 do not yet, and are listed under \"No visual test yet\" so the gap stays visible. Select a step, look at its picture, and set pass, fail or a note in the node panel. Generated from the roadmap and the Testing graph by scripts/offline/release-review-space.ts; edit those, not this file. Release status when generated: functional." ;
    hnav:order "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    p:has rev:wf-compare-v029, rev:wf-generated-assets, rev:wf-readme-path, rev:wf-reckoning-v029, rev:gap .

rev:wf-compare-v029 rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Read a note against what you hold, see it on the canvas, decide a contradiction" ;
    rdfs:comment "Part of v0.2.9: F300 F300 — One story, three ways to play: interactive, passive, recorded; a demo video is a story the device cannot run (status: planned). Adding a second note to a knowledge base that already holds a project is where it goes wrong quietly: the new note repeats some of what you have, words some of it differently, contradicts some, and adds some that is new. Here a check-in note is read against the Quick-Start example and lands in Review's compare flow, where each statement is labeled by what it would do. The same comparison is drawn over your own canvas, and the one contradiction, a moved deadline, is decided on its own card, with the replaced statement kept on record. Run by tests/e2e/workflow-compare-v029.test.ts. Also covers: F264 Review's compare and overlay screens — make them work, or remove them." ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets ;
    p:has rev:wf-compare-v029-01-extract-note, rev:wf-compare-v029-02-see-labels, rev:wf-compare-v029-03-see-on-canvas, rev:wf-compare-v029-04-decide-contradiction, rev:wf-compare-v029-05-see-on-record .

rev:wf-compare-v029-01-extract-note rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Extract statements from a second note" ;
    rdfs:comment "On the Add page title the note \"Phoenix check-in\" and paste: \"Notes from the Phoenix check-in: Project Phoenix is still in progress. Its deadline has moved to 2026-10-31. The content based filter trial is running. Carol is writing the vendor FAQ.\" Press Extract statements. You land in Review's compare flow, not in a separate screen.\n\nWhere: the Add page (/ingest).\n\nThe test checks: Extracting leaves the Add page and opens Review in compare mode with four statements." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/compare-v029/01-extract-note.webp" ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-compare-v029-02-see-labels ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-compare-v029-02-see-labels rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2. See each statement labeled by what it would do" ;
    rdfs:comment "Review shows the four statements the note brought, each against what you hold. One is a repeat of something you have, one is a near-duplicate worded differently, one contradicts a statement you hold, and one is new. The button says Accept new only, with the count of what it would settle.\n\nWhere: the Review page (/review).\n\nThe test checks: Exactly four entries carry the labels repeat, near-duplicate, contradiction and new, one of each, and the page says statements, never facts." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/compare-v029/02-see-labels.webp" ;
    hnav:order "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-compare-v029-03-see-on-canvas ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-compare-v029-01-extract-note ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-compare-v029-03-see-on-canvas rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3. See the comparison on your own canvas" ;
    rdfs:comment "The same comparison is drawn over your canvas. The new statement is a ghost in amber. The repeat is folded onto the statement you hold, the reinforcing one thickens what you hold, and the contradiction is a pair of statements shown side by side. The legend counts each. Nothing has been written to your knowledge base yet.\n\nWhere: the Review page (/review).\n\nThe test checks: The legend reads 1 new, drawn as ghosts, 1 repeat folded, 1 reinforcing and 1 contradiction; amber ghost pixels are on the canvas; the stored statements are still the confirmed ones plus four pending." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/compare-v029/03-see-on-canvas.webp" ;
    hnav:order "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-compare-v029-04-decide-contradiction ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-compare-v029-02-see-labels ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-compare-v029-04-decide-contradiction rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "4. Decide the contradiction where it is" ;
    rdfs:comment "The contradiction has a card of its own: the deadline you hold, 2026-09-15, against the 2026-10-31 from the new note. Choose take the new one, keep mine, or keep both. Take the new one confirms the new date.\n\nWhere: the Review page (/review).\n\nThe test checks: Both statements are readable on the card; after take the new one, 2026-10-31 is part of what you hold and 2026-09-15 is marked replaced." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/compare-v029/04-decide-contradiction.webp" ;
    hnav:order "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-compare-v029-05-see-on-record ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-compare-v029-03-see-on-canvas ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-compare-v029-05-see-on-record rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "5. See the replaced statement still on record" ;
    rdfs:comment "The decided pair stays on the page, marked replaced, still on record: the old deadline and the new one, with the note each came from. Keep mine would have rejected the arriving one instead, and keep both leaves the pair marked as a known disagreement.\n\nWhere: the Review page (/review).\n\nThe test checks: The settled pair reads replaced, still on record, and shows both deadlines; the stored rows are the old one superseded and the new one refined; the project's panel lists the new deadline under the check-in note and not the old one." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/compare-v029/05-see-on-record.webp" ;
    hnav:order "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-compare-v029-04-decide-contradiction ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2. Make pictures, clips and 3D splats on your own machine, and see them in a space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Part of v0.2.9: F300 F300 — One story, three ways to play: interactive, passive, recorded; a demo video is a story the device cannot run (status: planned). Write a prompt, and three local models turn it into a picture, then a short clip and a Gaussian splat (a 3D object drawn as many small soft blobs of color) made from that picture. You can turn a splat and look at it from any side. The results open as their own space, where each one sits on its own node, linked to what it was made from, and one splat can become the background of the space. Run by tests/e2e/workflow-generated-assets.test.ts." ;
    hnav:order "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-readme-path ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-compare-v029 ;
    p:has rev:wf-generated-assets-01-open-example, rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline, rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture, rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video, rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat, rev:wf-generated-assets-06-background .

rev:wf-generated-assets-01-open-example rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Open the Generated assets example as its own space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Under example data on the About page (or from the welcome page), choose Generated assets. It opens as a new space of its own and shows its graph, so trying it never mixes into the space you were working in. Opening it again refreshes that same space rather than making a second one.\n\nWhere: the About page (/about).\n\nThe test checks: The card offers to open the example as a space; choosing it lands on the graph of the new space, and the Spaces tab then shows Generated assets as the current space." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/01-open-example.webp" ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2. See the pipeline in the graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each result is a node, linked to what it was made from: a prompt to its picture, and the picture to its clip and its splat. Each node lists what its receipt recorded (the model, the seed, how long it took and when) under metadata in its details, not as extra nodes, and its license is a node of its own (MIT or Apache-2.0) that it links to. Turn on preview all to see every result on its node. A node with a splat is drawn inside its splat, which turns slowly.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: With previews on, at least three results show on their nodes (which ones are in view depends on where the layout puts them), and the 3D graph reports both node splats loaded and none failed." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/02-see-pipeline.webp" ;
    hnav:order "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-01-open-example ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3. The picture, made from a prompt" ;
    rdfs:comment "Z-Image-Turbo, run by stable-diffusion.cpp, turned the prompt into a 768×768 picture in eight steps. Find the picture's node (searching for its name works when it is out of view) and choose its preview to see it large. This picture is the starting point for the next two steps.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The picture the app shows is byte for byte the file its receipt describes (same SHA-256), its check accepted it, its models are MIT or Apache-2.0 licensed, and it opens large at 768 pixels wide." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/03-picture.webp" ;
    hnav:order "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "4. The clip, made from the picture" ;
    rdfs:comment "Wan2.2 TI2V-5B, also run by stable-diffusion.cpp, started from the picture and a second prompt describing the motion, and made a 49-frame clip. The check measures how much the last frame differs from the first, because a video model can return a clip in which almost nothing moves. When that happens the receipt says so rather than calling the clip fine.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The clip the app shows matches its receipt, its check accepted it, and it loads in the viewer at 512 pixels wide. The screenshot shows a frame from the middle of the clip." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/04-video.webp" ;
    hnav:order "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "5. The splat, made from the picture" ;
    rdfs:comment "TripoSplat turned the same picture into 32,768 Gaussians, writing a PLY file of about 2 MB. The first prompt asked for a flat carving seen from above, and TripoSplat made it as flat as a coin; asking for a three-quarter view with a domed shell gave it real depth. Choose the splat on its node to turn it and look at it from any side. Everything it shows on the far side of the turtle was guessed from one picture.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The splat the app shows matches its receipt and its check accepted it, and the viewer reports that it has loaded. The renderer is Gaussian-Splat-Lite, which the app loads only when a splat is on screen." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/05-splat.webp" ;
    hnav:order "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-06-background ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-06-background rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "6. Set a splat as the background of the space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open the lighthouse island splat and choose Set as background. The island is then drawn large behind the graph, sized to the graph and turning very slowly, and it never gets in the way of choosing a node. The choice is saved with the space, so it travels with an export. Clear background removes it.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The island splat matches its receipt. After Set as background the same control offers Clear background, which shows the setting was saved to the space, and the 3D graph reports three splats loaded and none failed: the two on their nodes and the island. Where the island sits and how it looks is shown by the screenshot, not measured by the test." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/06-background.webp" ;
    hnav:order "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-readme-path rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3. Add a source, review it, see it in a space, ask for a reckoning" ;
    rdfs:comment "Part of v0.2.9: F300 F300 — One story, three ways to play: interactive, passive, recorded; a demo video is a story the device cannot run (status: planned). The path the README describes, start to finish: put a short note into Reckons.AI, settle the claims it proposes, find them in your space, and ask for a reckoning that works from what you settled. It is the whole point of the product in five steps, and a browser test runs it on every change. Run by tests/e2e/workflow-readme-path.test.ts." ;
    hnav:order "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029 ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets ;
    p:has rev:wf-readme-path-01-add-source, rev:wf-readme-path-02-review-claims, rev:wf-readme-path-03-confirm-claims, rev:wf-readme-path-04-see-in-space, rev:wf-readme-path-05-reckoning .

rev:wf-readme-path-01-add-source rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Add a source" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open the Add tab, give the note a title, type or paste in a few sentences and press Extract statements. Reckons.AI reads the text and proposes claims from it. Nothing is accepted yet: every claim arrives waiting for your decision.\n\nWhere: the Add tab (/ingest).\n\nThe test checks: The Extract statements button is enabled once a title and text are entered, and pressing it takes the person off the Add tab when reading finishes. The test's stand-in reader returns placeholder claims at this point." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/readme-path/01-add-source.webp" ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-readme-path-02-review-claims ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-readme-path-02-review-claims rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2. Review the proposed claims" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open Review. Each claim waiting for a decision is a card. It names where the claim came from, shows the passage it was taken from, and offers accept, refine and reject. AI can misread what it reads, so this is where you check what it proposed against the original text.\n\nWhere: the Review tab (/review).\n\nThe test checks: At least one claim is waiting on the Review tab, shown as a card with accept, refine and reject buttons." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/readme-path/02-review-claims.webp" ;
    hnav:order "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-readme-path-03-confirm-claims ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-readme-path-01-add-source ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-readme-path-03-confirm-claims rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3. Confirm the claims that are right" ;
    rdfs:comment "Press accept on each claim that matches its source. You can also refine a claim or reject it. Only claims you confirm become part of the space; anything left waiting stays out.\n\nWhere: the Review tab (/review).\n\nThe test checks: Pressing accept settles the claims one by one until none of them is left waiting for a decision." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/readme-path/03-confirm-claims.webp" ;
    hnav:order "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-readme-path-04-see-in-space ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-readme-path-02-review-claims ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-readme-path-04-see-in-space rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "4. See the claims in your space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open Spaces. The claims you confirmed are now facts in your space, the collection of connected knowledge that everything you add feeds. The one you are working in is marked current, and its card says how many facts it holds.\n\nWhere: the Spaces tab (/kb).\n\nThe test checks: The Spaces tab shows the current one with more facts than it held before the claims were confirmed." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/readme-path/04-see-in-space.webp" ;
    hnav:order "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-readme-path-05-reckoning ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-readme-path-03-confirm-claims ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-readme-path-05-reckoning rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "5. Ask for a reckoning" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open Reckoning. Describe the situation in a sentence, press Next, say what outcome you want to reach and press Review, then Generate Proposal. Two options appear, each already written into your space as proposals: nothing is confirmed and no job has been queued until you accept one, and you weigh them yourself. It is a proposal to evaluate, not an answer to trust.\n\nWhere: the Reckoning page (/reckoning).\n\nThe test checks: Two option cards appear and the page says nothing is confirmed and no job has been queued. The reply in this run is scripted, written to read like a real reckoning about the Getting started notes; the test does not judge a real model's wording, which is measured separately." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/readme-path/05-reckoning.webp" ;
    hnav:order "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-readme-path-04-see-in-space ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029 rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "4. Reckon with chosen statements, then accept one option" ;
    rdfs:comment "Part of v0.2.9: F300 F300 — One story, three ways to play: interactive, passive, recorded; a demo video is a story the device cannot run (status: planned). A Reckoning helps you decide something using what your knowledge base already holds. Here the decision is how to unblock the data pipeline that the Quick-Start example's project depends on. You choose the statements that describe the situation, you choose what you are trying to get (an open question your knowledge base has, or an asset to make), and Reckons.AI writes two options into your knowledge base as proposals. Nothing in them counts until you accept one. Accepting is one confirmation: its statements become confirmed, any jobs it proposes are queued in a single approval, and the other option is marked superseded. If an option needs something it does not know yet, it is held as an open question; answering it finishes the proposal. Run by tests/e2e/workflow-reckoning-v029.test.ts. Also covers: F223.12 F223.12 — selections in, proposals out: a reckoning starts from chosen statements and targets, and writes its proposal into the space." ;
    hnav:order "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:gap ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-readme-path ;
    p:has rev:wf-reckoning-v029-01-select-on-canvas, rev:wf-reckoning-v029-02-choose-situation, rev:wf-reckoning-v029-03-choose-target, rev:wf-reckoning-v029-04-generate-proposal, rev:wf-reckoning-v029-05-show-on-canvas, rev:wf-reckoning-v029-06-accept-option, rev:wf-reckoning-v029-07-answer-missing-input .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-01-select-on-canvas rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Select statements on the canvas and reckon with them" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open the canvas and select Project Phoenix. A Reckon with these button appears in its panel. Press it: the Reckoning page opens with the statements that touch Project Phoenix already chosen.\n\nWhere: the canvas (/).\n\nThe test checks: With one entity selected the canvas offers Reckon with these, and pressing it opens the Reckoning page with at least one statement already chosen." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/01-select-on-canvas.webp" ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029-02-choose-situation ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-02-choose-situation rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2. Choose the situation from the list" ;
    rdfs:comment "On the Reckoning page the statements you hold are listed with a checkbox each. Untick any the canvas chose, tick the three that describe the decision, and write a sentence about it: \"We need to decide how to unblock the Phoenix data pipeline.\" The count says how many are chosen. Press Continue: the situation is saved as a Reckoning of its own, so reloading the page shows the same choice.\n\nWhere: the Reckoning page (/reckoning).\n\nThe test checks: Three statements are chosen, the count reads 3 statements chosen, and after Continue the address carries the Reckoning's id." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/02-choose-situation.webp" ;
    hnav:order "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029-03-choose-target ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-reckoning-v029-01-select-on-canvas ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-03-choose-target rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3. Choose the target: a question to answer" ;
    rdfs:comment "Choose Answer a question. The questions you still have open are listed; pick \"What does Data Pipeline v2 still need?\". The target is kept as a link to that statement, not as a copy of its words. Choosing an asset to make is the other option, and the page then shows the assets you have.\n\nWhere: the Reckoning page (/reckoning).\n\nThe test checks: The open question is listed and can be chosen; the review step then reads Answer this open question, and the choice is still there after a reload." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/03-choose-target.webp" ;
    hnav:order "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029-04-generate-proposal ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-reckoning-v029-02-choose-situation ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-04-generate-proposal rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "4. Generate a proposal that is written into your knowledge base" ;
    rdfs:comment "Press Review, then Generate proposal. Two options appear. Each is already in your knowledge base as proposals: a dashed statement saying what it would add, a proposed job that has not been queued, and a hollow question for the input it still needs. The page says so: nothing is confirmed and no job has been queued.\n\nWhere: the Reckoning page (/reckoning).\n\nThe test checks: Two option cards appear, every row the proposal wrote is pending, no job is queued, and each option has one statement, one job and one open question." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/04-generate-proposal.webp" ;
    hnav:order "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029-05-show-on-canvas ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-reckoning-v029-03-choose-target ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-05-show-on-canvas rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "5. Look at an option on the canvas" ;
    rdfs:comment "On an option's card press Show on the canvas. The canvas opens on that option alone, its proposed statements drawn dashed so they cannot be mistaken for what you hold. Use the control that stops showing one option to come back.\n\nWhere: the canvas (/).\n\nThe test checks: The address carries the option's focus, and the control that stops showing one proposal option is on the page." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/05-show-on-canvas.webp" ;
    hnav:order "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029-06-accept-option ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-reckoning-v029-04-generate-proposal ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-06-accept-option rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "6. Accept one option" ;
    rdfs:comment "Back on the Reckoning page press Accept on the first option. Before anything changes, a confirm step says how many statements will be confirmed, that one job will be queued in one approval, that the other option's rows will be marked superseded, and that one missing-input question stays open. Press the confirm button. The card says Accepted by you.\n\nWhere: the Reckoning page (/reckoning).\n\nThe test checks: The confirm step names the statement count, one job in one approval, the superseded rows and the open question; after it the accepted option's statement is confirmed, exactly one job request exists, and every row of the other option is superseded." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/06-accept-option.webp" ;
    hnav:order "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-reckoning-v029-07-answer-missing-input ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-reckoning-v029-05-show-on-canvas ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-reckoning-v029-07-answer-missing-input rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "7. Answer the missing input" ;
    rdfs:comment "The accepted option still has its open question. Type \"vendor-quote.pdf\" in its box and press Answer. The target of this Reckoning was that question, so answering it finishes the proposal and its standing reads Completed. No second job was queued.\n\nWhere: the Reckoning page (/reckoning).\n\nThe test checks: After Answer the proposal's standing reads Completed and the number of queued job requests is unchanged." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/reckoning-v029/07-answer-missing-input.webp" ;
    hnav:order "7"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-reckoning-v029-06-accept-option ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

